From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 21:17:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 065/105] fix(adaptive): give every runtime state its own
 draft-extend backend

This is the state-construction regression: with the steps=3 state merely
BUILT and never activated, code-edit acceptance fell 10.8 -> 5.7 and
throughput 564 -> 311 t/s.

Same root as the earlier illegal-memory-access fix. For compressed-QSA draft
models DraftBackendFactory.create_draft_extend_backend() (draft_utils.py:139)
returns draft_model_runner.attn_backend rather than a fresh backend, so every
state's draft-extend runner aliased one QwenSparseAttnBackend. That backend
caches captured graph metadata as

    self._cuda_graph_metadata[(forward_mode, bs)] = metadata

(qwen_sparse_attn_backend.py:1062) -- keyed by mode and batch size only, not
by the per-request token width, which for speculative-paged modes is
bs * num_draft_tokens. The steps=3 state's DRAFT_EXTEND_V2 capture therefore
replaced the launch state's entry with one sliced to 4 rows instead of 16.
The launch state then replayed its 16-wide draft-extend graph after filling
only 4 rows of QSA metadata: no crash (the stale rows hold in-range indices),
but the sparse selection seeding draft positions past the short state's width
is stale, so long chains stop being accepted -- short chains unaffected,
which is exactly the measured signature.

build_adaptive_runtime_state now builds a private draft-extend backend per
state (+0.14 GB); _override_worker_state already restored the launch one and
apply_runtime_state already swapped draft_runner.attn_backend, so the switch
path needed no change.

SGLANG_ADAPTIVE_SPLIT (debug only, default off) carries the bisection
switches that found this: no_draft, no_draft_graphs, no_target_graphs,
no_gdn_recovery, shared_extend (restores the old aliasing for A/B).

Config: adaptive_w16_3_15.json gains a "2" slot pinning bs>=2 to steps=15, so
the steps=3 state captures bs=1 graphs only.

Validation, one window, fnbench greedy repeats=2, needle PASS on all three:

  workload     W16          W4           adaptive     vs better fixed
  code-edit    10.38 / 483  3.86 / 332   9.57 / 504   +4%
  prose-en      2.78 / 141  2.51 / 228   2.59 / 218   -4%
  prose-ja      2.51 / 128  2.31 / 212   2.23 / 200   -6%
  agent-loop    4.78 / 230  3.29 / 291   3.46 / 276   -5%

dbg/FINDINGS.txt has the full bisection and the hypotheses ruled out.

